{"hw":"ἔλεγος","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ἔλεγος</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἔλεγος</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">ὁ</span>, <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">song, melody</b>, orig. accompanied by the flute, cf. <span class=\"gk\">ἄλυρος ἔ</span>. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hel.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">185</span> </span> (lyr.), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">146</span> </span> (lyr.); <span class=\"gk\">Ἀσίας ἔ. ἰήϊος</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hyps.Fr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3(1)i</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">ii9</span> </span>; so <span class=\"gk\">Ἔλεγοι</span>, title of a <span class=\"gk\">νόμος αὐλῳδικός</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Plu.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.1132d</span> </span>; of the <b class=\"lex-tr\">song</b> of the nightingale, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Av.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">218</span> </span>(pl.); <span class=\"gk\">ἔλεγον οἶτον</span>, of the halcyon, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1091</span> </span> (lyr.); later, <b class=\"lex-tr\">lament, song of mourning</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.R.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.782</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">poem in elegiac distichs</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Call.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Fr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">121</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἱλαροὶ ἔ</span>. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">AP</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">10.19</span> </span> (<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Apollonid.</span> </span>). (Commonly derived from <span class=\"gk\">ἒ ἒ λέγειν</span>, to cry woe! woe! <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">EM</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">326.49</span> </span>.)</div></div>"}